## Testing Strategy Overview

- Three-stage testing approach implementation
- Pre-commit quality gates enforcement
- Pre-push unit test validation
- CI integration test execution
- Coverage threshold requirements (60% minimum)
- Manual bypass for emergency situations

## Pre-commit Hook Workflow

- Format check with auto-fix
- Comprehensive lint analysis execution
- Debug statement detection and removal
- Dependency validation checks
- Parallel execution for speed optimization
- Stage fixed files automatically

```yaml
# Pre-commit format with auto-fix
dart-format:
  tags: quality
  glob: "**/*.dart"
  run: flutter format {staged_files} && git add {staged_files}
  stage_fixed: true
```

## Pre-push Testing Workflow

- Ensure dependencies are current
- Execute unit and widget tests
- Generate coverage reports automatically
- Verify test coverage thresholds
- Sequential execution for reliability
- Expanded test reporter output

```yaml
# Unit tests with coverage
unit-tests:
  tags: test
  run: flutter test --coverage --reporter=expanded
```

## Quality Gate Rules

- Fatal analysis with warnings enforcement
- No print statements in lib/
- No debugPrint statements in lib/
- Dependency consistency verification
- Conventional commit message format
- Security pattern detection

## Debug Statement Prevention

- Scan lib/ directory for print()
- Block debugPrint() in production code
- Replace with proper logging mechanisms
- Fail fast on detection
- Guide developers to alternatives
- Maintain clean production code

```yaml
# Debug print detection
no-debug-prints:
  run: |
    if grep -r "print(" lib/ --include="*.dart"; then
      echo "Remove print() statements before committing"
      exit 1
    fi
```

## Commit Message Standards

- Conventional commit format enforcement
- Support feat/fix/docs/style/refactor/test/chore types
- Optional scope specification allowed
- Clear descriptive commit messages
- Automated validation on commit-msg
- Team consistency maintenance

## Coverage Requirements

- Minimum 60% code coverage
- LCOV report generation automatically
- Coverage artifacts uploaded to CI
- Threshold validation in pipeline
- Coverage trend monitoring capability
- Quality metric tracking

```yaml
# Coverage threshold check
coverage-check:
  run: |
    if [ -f "coverage/lcov.info" ]; then
      echo "Test coverage report generated"
    fi
```

## Manual Testing Bypass

- Emergency override with LEFTHOOK=0
- Skip all hooks when needed
- Individual hook skipping support
- Team emergency procedures
- Documentation for bypass usage
- Restore normal workflow quickly

```bash
# Emergency bypass examples
LEFTHOOK=0 git commit -m "emergency fix"
LEFTHOOK=0 git push
```

